# "Push" and "release"

When William says the word, that is his approval for the whole flow below. Nothing else counts as approval to push.

## "Push" = open a PR and merge it through CI

`backend-ci.yml`, `frontend-ci.yml`, and `terraform-ci.yml` only run on pull requests into `main` that touch their paths, so a push straight to `main` skips CI. Never push to `main` directly. A PR that touches none of their paths (only `openspec/` or `.cursor/`) has no checks; that is expected.

1. Commit on a branch named for the change (`add-letter-tiles`), not on `main`. Add what a player or developer would notice to `CHANGELOG.md` under `## Unreleased` (`### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Fixed`) in the same PR.
2. Push the branch and `gh pr create --base main` with a summary and a test plan.
3. Watch `gh pr checks <n> --watch`. If a check fails, stop, read the log, and report the root cause. Do not merge a red PR.
4. When it's green, `gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch`. Use a merge commit so split commits stay separate; never squash or rebase.
5. Switch to `main` and `git pull --ff-only`.

## "Release" = publish a GitHub Release, which deploys to production

There is one environment: production. `release.yml` runs when a GitHub Release is published; a draft or a bare tag push does not ship. For each area that changed since the last release it calls that area's CD workflow (`*-cd.yml`, which runs its `*-ci.yml` first), in order: backend (API Worker), then frontend (web Worker, which binds to the API), then Terraform. A failure stops everything after it.

1. If there is unmerged work, "push" it first. Only release a commit that is on `origin/main` and has passed CI.
2. Pick the next version from `gh release list`. Default is a minor bump when `Unreleased` has `### Added` (`v0.1.0` → `v0.2.0`), otherwise a patch bump. Say which one you chose.
3. On a branch, rename `## Unreleased` to `## vX.Y.Z — YYYY-MM-DD` and put an empty `## Unreleased` above it. "Push" that.
4. Publish with that section as the notes:

   ```bash
   awk '/^## vX.Y.Z /{on=1; next} /^## /{on=0} on' CHANGELOG.md > /tmp/notes.md
   gh release create vX.Y.Z --target main --title vX.Y.Z --notes-file /tmp/notes.md
   ```

5. Watch the run until it ends: `gh run watch <id> --exit-status`. Report which areas shipped and which were skipped.

## Auth

Git's stored credential is `wgyasi`, and that account can't push to `williammgyasii/FriendsCorner`. Use the owner's CLI token for each command only; don't switch the active account or edit git config.

```bash
export GH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token --user williammgyasii)
git -c credential.helper= -c 'credential.helper=!gh auth git-credential' push -u origin HEAD
```

```
❌ "push" -> git push origin main
✅ "push" -> branch -> PR -> CI green -> merge commit -> pull main
❌ "release" -> git push origin v0.2.0   (a bare tag no longer ships)
✅ "release" -> (push if needed) -> CHANGELOG section -> gh release create v0.2.0 -> watch it finish
```
